#: src/configuring-languages.md:351
msgid "Formatting Selections"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:353
msgid ""
"Zed supports formatting only the selected text via `editor: format "
"selections` (<div>No default binding</div>). How this works depends on the "
"configured formatter:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:356
msgid ""
"The action is only shown when the active formatter can actually format "
"ranges for at least one selected buffer."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:358
msgid ""
"**Language server**: Sends an LSP range formatting request for each "
"selection. This provides the most precise selection-only formatting, and is "
"only available when the configured language server advertises range-"
"formatting support."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:361
msgid ""
"**Prettier**: Uses Prettier's built-in range formatting to format the "
"encompassing range of all selections. Any resulting edits that fall outside "
"the selected ranges are discarded, so only the selected code is modified."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:363
msgid ""
"**External commands**: External command formatters do not support range "
"formatting and are skipped when formatting selections."
msgstr ""

